	(footprint "Kycon_KPJX-4S-S"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "de296cb1-3c6d-54c1-b3c9-e1b1299fcd66")
		(at 150.9 118 90)
		(descr "Kycon KPJX-4S-S, 4-position shielded snap-and-lock DC power jack (power DIN), right angle THT, 7.5 A per pin at 48 V. Land from Kycon's own 'Recommended PCB Layout' (drawing KPJX-4S-S rev A17, 08/15/22), which is a BOTTOM view and is mirrored here. Origin = the centre of the NOSE FRONT; the mouth is +Y. Distances behind the nose front: shield tab 5.50, pegs and front shield legs 7.50, pins 3/4 11.00, pins 1/2 14.65, rear shield legs 16.00. Looking INTO the mouth, pin 1 is top left, 2 top right, 3 bottom left, 4 bottom right. F.Fab is the 16.0 x 13.4 BODY only: the O12.9 x 4.0 nose stands in front of it (src/board_geom.PANEL). Mates Kycon KPPX-4P, plug pin n on jack pin n. Mean Well's R7B plug numbers the contacts differently (its 1 and 2 are Kycon's 2 and 1): in Kycon's numbers the supply is +V on 2 and 4, -V on 1 and 3.")
		(tags "Kycon KPJX power DIN 4 pin snap lock DC jack THT")
